WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.105
Two ways to place an order. A

2
00:00:02.105 --> 00:00:05.750
market order prioritizes execution. A limit order

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.613
sets a price condition.

4
00:00:08.013 --> 00:00:11.198
Market: trade now. Sprout fills at its

5
00:00:11.198 --> 00:00:14.766
displayed simulated quote. Real market orders may

6
00:00:14.766 --> 00:00:16.623
fill at a different price.

7
00:00:17.023 --> 00:00:19.297
Buy limit: at or below. With a

8
00:00:19.297 --> 00:00:22.053
$100 buy limit, the purchase can

9
00:00:22.053 --> 00:00:24.811
fill at $100 or less. It

10
00:00:24.811 --> 00:00:27.406
cannot fill above $100.

11
00:00:27.815 --> 00:00:29.863
A limit may never fill. If the

12
00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.741
price stays above $100, that buy

13
00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:35.306
limit waits. A chosen price is not a

14
00:00:35.306 --> 00:00:36.774
guaranteed trade.

15
00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.605
Practice both. Sprout checks pending limits while

16
00:00:40.605 --> 00:00:42.961
the app is open. Real trading has

17
00:00:42.961 --> 00:00:45.920
spreads, slippage, and other costs.

